        <mxCell id="p1n10" parent="1" style="sketch=0;outlineConnect=0;fontColor=#232F3E;gradientColor=#F54749;gradientDirection=north;fillColor=#C7131F;strokeColor=#ffffff;dashed=0;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11;aspect=fixed;shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.secrets_manager;fontStyle=1;labelWidth=130;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="Secrets Manager ARNs (never inlined)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="68" width="68" x="350" y="490" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1n11" parent="1" style="sketch=0;outlineConnect=0;fontColor=#232F3E;gradientColor=#F34482;gradientDirection=north;fillColor=#BC1356;strokeColor=#ffffff;dashed=0;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=11;aspect=fixed;shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.systems_manager;fontStyle=1;labelWidth=130;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="SSM parameter ARNs" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="68" width="68" x="550" y="490" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - Reusable Terraform building blocks for serverless AWS infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;How they are used&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Root stacks compose API, compute, data, events, IAM, encryption and configuration primitives.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Every pattern module is built from these four primitives - nothing else creates raw resources.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Modules accept artefact references (S3 locations, image URIs, ARNs) and settings; they never package application code.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Required tags (Environment, System, Owner) are validated on every primitive.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1320" x="40" y="745" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="Pattern Icons" id="pattern-icons">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1450" pageHeight="920" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="leg_title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" value="Pattern icons - the subsystem component alphabet" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="800" x="40" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg_intro" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;What this page is&lt;/b&gt; - every pattern in the library condensed into a single recognisable glyph&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;How to read a glyph&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;b&gt;grey tab&lt;/b&gt; names the pattern; one glyph always corresponds to one Terraform module instance (the [bracketed] caption maps to modules/patterns/*).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;b&gt;tiles&lt;/b&gt; are the AWS resources the pattern is built from, placed in flow order.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;b&gt;blue words&lt;/b&gt; are the role each resource plays, using the book&#39;s vocabulary (command, db, trigger, collect, emit, ingress, egress...).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Where they are used&lt;/b&gt; - the worked example pages (Online Order Subsystem, Payments Payout Process) compose these glyphs into complete applications, and every pattern tab carries its glyph as a badge in the top-right corner. Each glyph deliberately hides the finer wiring - the Lambdas, queues, DLQs, IAM roles and KMS keys - which lives on that pattern&#39;s own tab." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="180" width="1370" x="40" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lg_eventhub_body" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#C9CDD1;" value="" vertex="1">
