        <mxCell id="p2e6" edge="1" parent="1" source="p2n7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;" target="p2n8" value="P1. filter_pattern">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2e7" edge="1" parent="1" source="p2n8" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;" target="p2n9" value="P2. deliberate point-to-point delivery">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - A subsystem event backbone for many-to-many event collaboration.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Producer services publish facts to the custom EventBridge bus with PutEvents.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Each route rule pattern-matches the events it cares about.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The rule delivers matched events to its consumer targets (Lambda, SQS, Firehose, Step Functions...), assuming a target role where the service requires one.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;A&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The optional archive records everything that crosses the bus for later replay.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Deliveries EventBridge cannot complete dead-letter to a per-target SQS DLQ (auto-created when none is supplied), so no event is silently dropped. Consumer-side processing failures are handled by each consumer&#39;s own DLQ (see the BFF and Control pages).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Variant&lt;/b&gt; - &lt;b&gt;P1-P2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; EventBridge Pipes give deliberate point-to-point delivery with filtering. The source must be a pollable channel (SQS, Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, MQ, MSK); the target can be any consumer. Use a pipe only where one producer channel feeds exactly one known consumer." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1320" x="40" y="745" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tg_eventhub_body" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#C9CDD1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="94" width="102" x="1258" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
