        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3e6" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3n5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#C7131F;strokeColor=#C7131F;dashed=1;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p3n6" value="F1. failed stream records to trigger DLQ">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3e7" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3n3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p3n10" value="4. PutEvents (task events, optional)">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="654" y="60" />
              <mxPoint x="1274" y="60" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3e8" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3n10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p3n7" value="7. hub rule routes inbound events">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="0.5847" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="1274" y="690" />
              <mxPoint x="654" y="690" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3e9" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3n7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p3n9" value="8. batched consume (ESM, batch 10)">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3e10" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3n7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#C7131F;strokeColor=#C7131F;dashed=1;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p3n8" value="F2. poison messages to listener DLQ">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3e11" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3n9" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p3n4" value="9. materialise view">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="374" y="690" />
              <mxPoint x="320" y="690" />
              <mxPoint x="320" y="280" />
              <mxPoint x="850" y="280" />
              <mxPoint x="850" y="194" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - A frontend-specific backend that owns request composition and read-model materialisation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; HTTPS requests reach the HTTP API.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Each route invokes the REST handler under a per-route permission.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The handler reads and writes the owned table.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; It may also publish task events directly to the hub.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Committed table changes flow through the DynamoDB stream to an event source mapping (ESM) - the managed poller that connects a stream or queue to Lambda - which invokes the trigger.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The trigger publishes database-first facts to the hub.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;7&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; A hub rule routes inbound events to the listener queue.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;8&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; An ESM invokes the listener in batches of 10 with ReportBatchItemFailures, so only failed messages are retried - not the whole batch.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;9&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The listener materialises the view back into the table.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Stream records that exhaust their retries land in the trigger DLQ via the on_failure destination.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; A poison message redrives to the listener DLQ after maxReceiveCount attempts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - The frontend talks to the BFF, never directly to subsystem data stores or downstream services. All queues, the table and logs are encrypted with the module&#39;s customer-managed KMS key." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1320" x="40" y="745" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
