        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4e10" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4n10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;dashed=1;fontStyle=1;" target="p4n9" value="credentials / configuration">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4e11" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4n10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;dashed=1;" target="p4n3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="350" y="624" />
              <mxPoint x="350" y="174" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p4desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - An anti-corruption gateway that isolates external systems from subsystem services.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The external system calls the optional webhook API.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The API invokes the ingress adapter.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The adapter normalises the payload and publishes subsystem events to the hub.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The egress rule matches outbound integration events on the hub.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Matched events are enqueued on the egress queue.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; An event source mapping (ESM) invokes the egress adapter in batches with ReportBatchItemFailures, so only failed messages are retried.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;7&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The adapter translates and calls the external API using credentials resolved from Secrets Manager / SSM at runtime.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Deliveries EventBridge cannot complete dead-letter to the rule-target DLQ.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; A poison message redrives to the egress DLQ after maxReceiveCount attempts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - Credentials, retries, protocol mapping and external failure handling stay inside the ESG. External schemas never leak onto the hub." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1320" x="40" y="745" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tg_esg_body" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#C9CDD1;" value="" vertex="1">
