        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5e7" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5n7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p5n8" value="5. stream consume (ESM)">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5e8" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5n8" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#C7131F;strokeColor=#C7131F;dashed=1;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1" target="p5n9" value="F3. failed stream records to trigger DLQ">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5e9" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5n8" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p5n1" value="6. PutEvents (higher-order events)">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="864" y="680" />
              <mxPoint x="114" y="680" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p5desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - A control service that derives higher-order events from observed lower-order events.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The hub delivers lower-order events matching the listener rule.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The rule routes them onto the listener queue.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; An event source mapping (ESM) - the managed poller that connects SQS to Lambda - invokes the listener in batches of 10 with ReportBatchItemFailures, so only failed messages are retried.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The listener collects and correlates state in the private micro event store.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The table stream feeds a second ESM that invokes the trigger.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The trigger evaluates the accumulated state and publishes higher-order decision events back to the hub.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Deliveries EventBridge cannot complete dead-letter to the rule-target DLQ.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; A poison message redrives to the listener DLQ after maxReceiveCount attempts.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Stream records that exhaust their retries land in the trigger DLQ.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - Control state is private; other services see decisions only as events on the hub." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1320" x="40" y="745" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tg_control_r_body" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#C9CDD1;" value="" vertex="1">
