        <mxCell id="p7desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - An immutable analytical record of selected subsystem facts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; An event_hub route delivers matching facts to the Firehose delivery stream.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Firehose writes compressed, KMS-encrypted objects to the versioned, Object-Locked S3 bucket.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Analytics and replay consumers read from the lake without touching operational services.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Failed Firehose deliveries are written under error_output_prefix and logged to CloudWatch; a delivery-failure alarm raises the alert.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - The routing rule itself belongs to the event hub, not this module. Object Lock (GOVERNANCE) means archived facts cannot be deleted or overwritten within the retention window." vertex="1">
