        <mxCell id="p9desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - The minimal autonomous-subsystem starting point.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Composition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This stack instantiates exactly two pattern modules: event_hub (with no routes configured) and bff_service.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;User intent enters through the BFF; table changes become facts on the hub via the change trigger.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Control services, gateways, the event lake and operational monitors are deliberately not part of this stack - they attach later through hub routes (see the Public App Stack and the worked examples).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - Owned data remains inside the subsystem; other capabilities integrate through events." vertex="1">
