        <mxCell id="p10e6" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10n2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;jettySize=auto;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;dashed=1;" target="p10n7" value="standard logs (optional)">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="514" y="240" />
              <mxPoint x="414" y="240" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10e7" edge="1" parent="1" source="p10n8" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;jettySize=auto;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;dashed=1;endArrow=none;" target="p10n3" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p10desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - A secure edge entry point for frontend artefacts and API routing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The browser reaches the CloudFront distribution over HTTPS (TLSv1.2_2021; HSTS, frame-deny and nosniff response headers; 403/404 rewritten to /index.html for the SPA).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Static paths are served from the private S3 origin through Origin Access Control with SigV4 signing; the bucket policy admits only this distribution (aws:SourceArn) and denies insecure transport.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; /api/* path patterns route to BFF HTTP API origins with caching disabled and the host header stripped.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure path&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; An optional secondary origin takes over automatically when the primary returns 500/502/503/504 (origin group failover).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - CloudFront and the ACM certificate must be created in us-east-1 (validated by the module). Access logging is optional and needs an ACL-enabled bucket - the legacy logging stack predates OAC." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1320" x="40" y="745" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tg_frontendedge_body" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#C9CDD1;" value="" vertex="1">
