        <mxCell id="p11e5" edge="1" parent="1" source="p11n2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p11n6" value="OR rule">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11e6" edge="1" parent="1" source="p11n6" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p11n7" value="notify">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11e7" edge="1" parent="1" source="p11n7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p11n8" value="page">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p11desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - A regional readiness signal for failover decisions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Per-dependency CloudWatch metric alarms wrap each AWS dependency the subsystem relies on.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Each alarm backs a Route 53 CLOUDWATCH_METRIC child health check (LastKnownStatus on missing data).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; A calculated check aggregates the children - the threshold defaults to all children healthy - and drives DNS failover.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The composite alarm fans the same signal to on-call.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - The check represents subsystem readiness rather than raw endpoint uptime. A CloudWatch Synthetics canary in the opposite region is the recommended traffic source but lives outside this module." vertex="1">
