        <mxCell id="p12e6" edge="1" parent="1" source="p12n2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#C7131F;strokeColor=#C7131F;dashed=1;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p12n7" value="failed delivery (dead_letter_config)">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12e7" edge="1" parent="1" source="p12n8" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;fontStyle=1;" target="p12n5" value="alarm_actions">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12e8" edge="1" parent="1" source="p12n4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;jettySize=auto;dashed=1;fontStyle=1;" target="p12n9" value="read for replay">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p12desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;Intent&lt;/b&gt; - An independent monitor for fault events and operational failure signals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; A dedicated EventBridge rule matches fault-typed events on the hub.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; It fans them to Firehose for partitioned, versioned S3 archival.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; And to the SNS topic for on-call notification.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A fault-arrival alarm fires on any matched event; a DLQ-depth alarm catches delivery failures.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;An out-of-band CLI replays archived events once the root cause is fixed.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;F1&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Both targets share an SQS DLQ, so no fault is silently lost.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Boundary&lt;/b&gt; - Monitoring remains outside individual services so one service failure does not hide another." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1320" x="40" y="745" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tg_faultmon_body" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2F3F4;strokeColor=#C9CDD1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="94" width="142" x="1218" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
