        <mxCell id="ob_desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;How the glyphs compose for this domain&lt;/b&gt; (each glyph hides the finer wiring - Lambdas, queues, DLQs, streams - shown on that pattern&#39;s own tab).&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Customer journey&lt;/b&gt; - CloudFront (frontend_edge) serves the micro-frontend shell whose master manifests come from the manifest deployer (micro_frontend).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Micro-apps&lt;/b&gt; - each user activity has its own BFF (bff_service): five separate API Gateways unified behind one domain via frontend_edge.api_origins, one cache behaviour per path_pattern. Each team deploys independently.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Event backbone&lt;/b&gt; - each BFF table publishes business facts onto the subsystem bus (event_hub) through its stream trigger; consumers subscribe to what they need and emit results back, so collaboration stays asynchronous with no direct service-to-service calls. The Tracking BFF is read-only: its view table is materialised from hub events (CQRS).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;External integration&lt;/b&gt; - the Payments and Shipping gateways (esg_service) are anti-corruption boundaries around Stripe and DHL.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Operations&lt;/b&gt; - the event lake keeps the immutable audit trail; the fault monitor catches fault-typed events for resubmission; observability_baseline and regional_health_check watch every service above.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="1660" x="40" y="1060" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
