        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="po_c15" edge="1" parent="1" source="po_obs_body" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;jettySize=auto;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=#545B64;dashed=1;" target="po_health_body" value="alarm fan-out">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="po_desc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#D5DBDB;fontColor=#2B3A42;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Segoe UI;arcSize=4;gradientColor=#E6E6E6;gradientDirection=north;" value="&lt;b&gt;An autonomous payouts subsystem assembled entirely from the pattern glyphs&lt;/b&gt; (each glyph hides the finer wiring - Lambdas, queues, DLQs, streams - shown on that pattern&#39;s own tab).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Flow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;1-2&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Ops initiate a payout through the Initiation BFF behind the portal CDN.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The write to its table publishes PayoutRequested through the stream trigger.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;4-5&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; Compliance and Risk Screening (control_service, reactor) checks sanctions, limits and balances, then emits PayoutApproved or PayoutRejected.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;6-7&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The Execution Saga (control_service, Step Functions) orchestrates the transfer with waits, retries and compensation, emitting TransferInstructed.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;8-11&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The Banking Rails Gateway (esg_service) makes the idempotent call to the partner bank and normalises settlement / return webhooks back into TransferSettled / TransferReturned events.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;12&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp; The read-only Tracking BFF view is materialised from those events (CQRS).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;b&gt;Payments-specific notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;The event lake Object-Locked bucket is the immutable regulatory audit trail.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The fault monitor catches fault-typed events (rejected instructions, unmatched settlements) for operator resubmission.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Every hop carries a DLQ, so no payout instruction is silently lost.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Idempotency keys must travel in the event detail so retries at any layer (EventBridge, SQS redrive, saga retry, bank API) never double-pay.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="300" width="1660" x="40" y="1140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
